<title>LATVIA: SOME 84 PCT OF UNIBANKA SHARES BLOCKED.</title>
<headline>SOME 84 PCT OF UNIBANKA SHARES BLOCKED.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Riga stock exchange on Monday said that some 84 percent of Unibanka shares have been blocked ahead of its shareholders' meeting on June 2.</p>
<p>The bouse said in a statement that 16.78 million shares were blocked out of total registered stock of 19.91 million.</p>
<p>The meeting is due to decide on whether a controversial merger between Zemes Bank and Unibanka should go ahead.</p>
<p>Shares have to be blocked ahead of a meeting for the shareholders to participate in the voting on resolutions.</p>
<p>The bourse gave the following list of Unibanka's shareholders, compiled on May 22.</p>
<p>    SHAREHOLDER				   PCT OF SHARES</p>
<p>    The privatisation agency		     33.33</p>
<p>    EBRD						 20.09</p>
<p>    Hansapank					   7.53</p>
<p>    Swedfund International AB		     7.53</p>
<p>    bin Ibrahim Al-Ibrahim Sheikh Majid	 5.62</p>
<p>    Parekss Bank					3.32</p>
<p>    Baltic Fund Securities Latvia		 1.17</p>
<p>    Oppenheimer &amp; Co.Inc			    1.03</p>
<p>    Amiel Financial Services			1.03</p>
<p>    Zemes Bank					  0.74</p>
<p>    Others (hold less than 0.5 pct)	     2.78</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
